2. Individual plan: free personal, noncommercial use

An individual natural person may download, install, run, copy and modify
Diffrook without paying a license fee solely for that person's private,
personal, noncommercial activities. Each Individual installation is limited
to one registered user account and three saved automations. Disabled
automations also count toward the limit. Multiple accounts, shared accounts
and splitting an organizational deployment into personal installations do not
qualify as Individual use.

The Individual plan does not permit use for a company, organization or team,
or use in employment, freelance work, consulting, client work or other
professional or commercial activities, even when only one person uses
Diffrook or no fee is charged for a particular task. Those uses require a
Business license. The user's own hosting, infrastructure and AI-provider costs
remain the user's responsibility.

3. Business plan: paid self-hosted use

Companies, organizations, teams and individuals performing professional or
commercial work must obtain a separate paid Business license from Alexandre
Ramos or an authorized Diffrook licensor before operating Diffrook for those
purposes. A Business license authorizes self-hosted use only within the
customer, installation, user, automation and term limits specified in the
applicable written commercial agreement. Fees, duration, renewal, support and
any service commitments are determined by that agreement; no particular price,
perpetual entitlement, support level or unlimited allowance is promised here.

A signed license file activates the purchased installation's technical
entitlements. Possessing source code, setting an environment variable,
altering the database or disabling a technical check does not grant a Business
license. Technical limits do not replace the restrictions in these terms or
the applicable commercial agreement. Specific terms in a signed commercial
agreement prevail over conflicting terms in this license for that customer.

On expiry or removal of a Business license, its additional technical creation
allowances cease. Stored data is not automatically deleted. Continued access
for reading, editing, deleting or exporting existing data does not extend a
customer's contractual entitlement to operate Diffrook for business use.

4. Hosted subscriptions and third-party hosting

The licensor may offer a separately paid subscription in which the licensor
hosts and operates Diffrook for the customer. A hosted subscription is distinct
from a self-hosted Business license. Availability, features, infrastructure,
usage limits, pricing, billing, data handling, support and termination are
subject to a separate hosted-service agreement. This license does not promise
that a hosted service is currently available or included in a self-hosted fee.

Operating, reselling or offering Diffrook as a hosted or managed service for
third parties requires separate written authorization from the licensor.
Neither the Individual plan nor a standard self-hosted Business license grants
that right. The licensor's own authorized hosted offerings are permitted.

